# No "tap tempo" branding

**Hard rule (product owner, repeated):** BPM Tap must **never** use the phrase **tap tempo** (any casing) in user-facing copy, titles, H1, meta, OG, FAQ, guides, UI labels, schema, `llms.txt`, or marketing.

## Why

- [taptempo.io](https://taptempo.io/) is a **competitor brand / exact-match domain**.
- Using their phrase on our site dilutes our brand and points users/search toward their name.

## Allowed language

Prefer our terms:

- Tap BPM
- BPM counter
- BPM tap
- find / measure BPM
- tempo (alone is OK when musical, e.g. “song tempo”)
- metronome, delay, mic listen

## Forbidden

- `tap tempo`, `Tap Tempo`, `tap-tempo` in copy or new public URLs/slugs
- Guides or titles like “Tap tempo vs …”
- Targeting competitor brand as our primary keyword in on-page SEO
- Mentions of taptempo.io on the **live site** (strategy docs may name competitors for analysis only)

## Exceptions

- Legacy **301 redirects** from old paths that already contain `tap-tempo` in the URL (keep redirecting away; do not recreate those pages).
- Internal strategy notes may discuss the competitor by domain when analyzing SERP — never as copy to ship.

## Check before shipping

If a change adds copy/meta/slug, search the diff for `tap tempo` / `tap-tempo` / `taptempo`. Zero hits on public surfaces.
